alacritty 0.17.0 on powerpc-apple-darwin (Mac OS X 10.6.8, OpenGL 2.1 context): the GLES2 renderer, which alacritty
falls back to below GLSL 3.3, prepends `#version 100` to shaders written with ES precision qualifiers, and the desktop
GLSL compiler of 10.6 rejects both: `Error: Render(Shader(Compile("ERROR: 0:1: '' :  Version number not supported by
GL2 / ERROR: 0:25: 'highp' : syntax error")))`. On PowerPC the header is `#version 110` plus empty `highp`/`mediump`/`lowp`
macros (the shaders use no `precision` statement and nothing beyond GLSL 1.10: attribute/varying, texture2D, mod, floor).
Port patch, not a crate patch: `patch -p1` on the GitHub tarball (alacritty/src/renderer/shader.rs), `-p2` on the
crates.io crate (src/renderer/shader.rs).

--- alacritty/src/renderer/shader.rs
+++ alacritty/src/renderer/shader.rs
@@ -22,6 +22,12 @@
     fn shader_header(&self) -> &'static str {
         match self {
             Self::Glsl3 => "#version 330 core\n",
+            // Mac OS X 10.6 (PowerPC) is desktop OpenGL 2.x: its GLSL has neither the ES `#version 100` nor
+            // the precision qualifiers (`'highp' : syntax error`), so the GLES2 shaders are built as GLSL 1.10
+            // with the qualifiers defined away.
+            Self::Gles2 if cfg!(any(target_arch = "powerpc", target_arch = "powerpc64")) => {
+                "#version 110\n#define GLES2_RENDERER\n#define highp\n#define mediump\n#define lowp\n"
+            },
             Self::Gles2 => "#version 100\n#define GLES2_RENDERER\n",
         }
     }

alacritty 0.17.0 on powerpc-apple-darwin (Mac OS X 10.6.8, OpenGL 2.1): `thread main panicked: gl function was not loaded`
in gl::BindVertexArray under Gles2Renderer::new. 10.6's GL 2.1 has vertex array objects only as GL_APPLE_vertex_array_object;
gl_generator (Fallbacks::All) finds glGenVertexArrays/glDeleteVertexArrays through the registry aliases
glGenVertexArraysAPPLE/glDeleteVertexArraysAPPLE, but glBindVertexArrayAPPLE is not an alias (binding 0 selects the default
array there, which is exactly how the renderers use it), so it is loaded by hand right after gl::load_with.
Second hunk of the same port patch.

--- alacritty/src/renderer/mod.rs
+++ alacritty/src/renderer/mod.rs
@@ -128,6 +128,15 @@
                 let symbol = CString::new(symbol).unwrap();
                 gl_display.get_proc_address(symbol.as_c_str()).cast()
             });
+            // Mac OS X 10.6 (PowerPC) OpenGL 2.1: vertex array objects come from GL_APPLE_vertex_array_object;
+            // the registry aliases glGen/DeleteVertexArraysAPPLE to the core names but not glBindVertexArrayAPPLE
+            // (binding 0 there selects the default array, which is what the renderers want), so load it by hand.
+            if cfg!(any(target_arch = "powerpc", target_arch = "powerpc64")) && !gl::BindVertexArray::is_loaded() {
+                gl::BindVertexArray::load_with(|_| {
+                    let symbol = CString::new("glBindVertexArrayAPPLE").unwrap();
+                    gl_display.get_proc_address(symbol.as_c_str()).cast()
+                });
+            }
         }
 
         let shader_version = gl_get_string(gl::SHADING_LANGUAGE_VERSION, "shader version")?;

alacritty 0.17.0 on powerpc-apple-darwin (Mac OS X 10.6.8, OpenGL 2.1), third hunk: the GLES2 text shader declares its
five attributes (cellCoords, glyphCoords, uv, textColor, backgroundColor) and the rect shader its two (aPos, aColor)
without a location, while the vertex setup passes them to glVertexAttribPointer as 0..4 / 0..1 in declaration order;
nothing binds them, and a GLSL linker may assign them in any order. Symptom on the G5: cell backgrounds (pass 0:
cellCoords + backgroundColor) and rects draw, every glyph pass draws nothing, including alacritty's own builtin
box-drawing bitmaps. Fix: glBindAttribLocation before glLinkProgram for the names the vertex shader contains.
The GLSL3 shaders' `layout(location)` give the same numbers, so this is a no-op there; not PowerPC-gated.

--- alacritty/src/renderer/shader.rs
+++ alacritty/src/renderer/shader.rs
@@ -40,6 +40,20 @@ impl ShaderProgram {
         vertex_shader: &'static str,
         fragment_shader: &'static str,
     ) -> Result<Self, ShaderError> {
+        // The GLES2 shaders declare their attributes without a location and the vertex setup assumes declaration
+        // order, but a GLSL linker may assign them in any order.
+        let attributes: Vec<(GLuint, &CStr)> = [
+            (0, c"cellCoords"),
+            (1, c"glyphCoords"),
+            (2, c"uv"),
+            (3, c"textColor"),
+            (4, c"backgroundColor"),
+            (0, c"aPos"),
+            (1, c"aColor"),
+        ]
+        .into_iter()
+        .filter(|(_, name)| vertex_shader.contains(name.to_str().unwrap()))
+        .collect();
         let vertex_shader =
             Shader::new(shader_version, shader_header, gl::VERTEX_SHADER, vertex_shader)?;
         let fragment_shader =
@@ -51,6 +65,9 @@ impl ShaderProgram {
         unsafe {
             gl::AttachShader(program.id(), vertex_shader.id());
             gl::AttachShader(program.id(), fragment_shader.id());
+            for &(location, name) in &attributes {
+                gl::BindAttribLocation(program.id(), location, name.as_ptr());
+            }
             gl::LinkProgram(program.id());
             gl::GetProgramiv(program.id(), gl::LINK_STATUS, &mut success);
         }
